2026-11-07T06:35:58.6612410Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T06:35:58.6638850Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T06:35:58.6639650Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T06:35:58.6640060Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T06:35:58.6640350Z 
2026-11-07T06:35:58.6640560Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T06:35:58.6640780Z 
2026-11-07T06:35:58.6640960Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T06:35:58.6641460Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T06:35:58.6641690Z 
2026-11-07T06:35:58.6642000Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T06:35:58.6642380Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T06:35:58.6642680Z 
2026-11-07T06:35:58.6642930Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T06:35:58.6643430Z   $ sh ./install-nix
